WEBVTT

00:01.840 --> 00:05.040
So now, let's change the role to an employee,

00:05.360 --> 00:10.400
for example, Henrik. Of course, Henrik doesn't

00:10.400 --> 00:13.600
have the same rights as a manager.

00:14.640 --> 00:16.840
He cannot change the schedule. But of course,

00:17.000 --> 00:20.920
he can see his schedule and his colleagues'.

00:21.560 --> 00:25.320
So let's take a day, for example, the 23rd of November:

00:25.560 --> 00:27.800
Henrik starts at 7:30.

00:28.360 --> 00:33.040
But Henrik would like to start at 9:30, because he has

00:33.040 --> 00:35.200
an important thing to do, for example.

00:35.360 --> 00:37.840
So, Henrik can send a request.

00:39.360 --> 00:42.720
He can click on "My requests" and send it here.

00:43.360 --> 00:47.280
You can write pretty much anything,

00:47.600 --> 00:50.040
for example: "Can I start later on Monday?"

00:50.280 --> 00:52.440
"I can't work next week."

00:52.760 --> 00:57.320
Usually, these requests are sent by text message,

00:57.320 --> 00:59.720
on a piece of paper, or in the corridor.

00:59.960 --> 01:03.960
With ShiftSmith, employees write their requests

01:04.560 --> 01:07.520
in their own words. So let's say,

01:07.760 --> 01:13.040
for example, this sentence: "On Monday 23/11,

01:13.360 --> 01:16.640
I would like to start working at 9:30."

01:16.880 --> 01:20.000
I click on "Parse", and this sends the request

01:20.520 --> 01:23.880
to the manager. And what does this sentence mean?

01:24.120 --> 01:28.840
It means that he would like to change his shift

01:28.840 --> 01:33.400
from A to E. So let's change the role

01:33.400 --> 01:34.420
and go to the manager position.

01:34.670 --> 01:39.110
I click on "Constraints", and here I can see Henrik's request.

01:40.230 --> 01:44.950
Here, I can see that he would like to be on shift E.

01:45.510 --> 01:48.030
So I can either reject it or approve it.

01:48.350 --> 01:53.310
If I approve it, I can write the new shift for Henrik

01:53.870 --> 01:57.790
into my draft, or directly into the published version.

01:58.110 --> 02:02.110
I'd like to approve it on the draft, to see whether

02:02.630 --> 02:05.670
it changes. I go to "Schedule".

02:05.990 --> 02:08.310
Here, this is the published version.

02:08.630 --> 02:12.710
I click here, on the draft, and on the 23rd,

02:12.790 --> 02:17.350
I can see that Henrik is now on shift E, and it's locked.

02:17.390 --> 02:22.030
So now, the solver will not change it,

02:22.190 --> 02:24.420
because now it's marked as locked.

02:24.610 --> 02:28.050
And if a request has no date,

02:28.570 --> 02:31.450
ShiftSmith refuses it,

02:31.770 --> 02:35.100
so nothing unclear ever gets into your schedule.
